; C13a  Winning 42 p. 44 (W42-p044-c) and p. 48 (W42-p048-d); played in
; Hands 32 and 33 (pp. 109, 111)
; Rule, in our words: a setter with no trump, when the bidder leads trump,
; throws a tile that is his only one of some suit (not a count tile), so that
; he is void there when the bidder's off comes.
; Python gate (pour_setter gate_c13a): a setter, the bidder led trump, the
; mover holds no trump; the book's tiles are the non-count tiles that are the
; mover's only tile of one of their pip suits.
; How this encoding differs: it cannot say "his only one of that suit" and
; allows every non-count tile. It is the gate's superset.
; Out of trump is read from the hand, as in C1b.
; GAP declarer: the bidder is written in as S0.
; GAP none: "the only tile I hold of suit q" is "no other tile of mine follows
; q", a negated existential.
(policy c13a-shed-a-singleton
  (initial play)
  (fallback lowest-legal)
  (rule throw-a-lone-tile (in play) (next play) (select answer)
    (guard
      (query
        (roles (chair me) (domino lone) (context suit))
        (out lone)
        (pattern
          (viewer me)
          (opponent me S0)
          (leader S0)
          (led-context q*)
          (own-legal lone)
          (not (in lone q*))
          (count lone 0)
          (in lone suit)
          (not (context suit q*))
          ; GAP none: (none (own-legal other) (in other suit)) for another tile other
          )))))
